[{:db/id "q-117662/selection/ab203d967d195ff54da44904f652521d55f66b5a377e2ecb487084891d40fd32" :answer/id #uuid "0ef29137-7eda-5851-8e87-4646450e55ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "122" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117662/selection/e9fe4f903064948e90ac9e041d7548aaeba35bf685b20db89d2f19dbf50f8a32" :answer/id #uuid "5d6443d4-e468-5b46-9a8a-cef9c464313e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1115" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117662/selection/362d6474c6f01bbd84dd4aad1f36df5c29d2ebafec9135e07e89e7292a2cd334" :answer/id #uuid "b73702a1-67af-5e22-b65d-37f5dd1929fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "101" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117662/selection/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" :answer/id #uuid "1a34c67c-e9c3-5a6f-b1c0-6fbfca30fdb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117662/selection/aa56327b5902f25e2f7d95c792ef03ce1de9c18c97e2a74df0ef0eb1b77ad0a2" :answer/id #uuid "942c0acf-063c-5f10-bf3b-6caeeb36c5bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "127" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117662/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ff15138-2413-54b3-b8ab-034b626452de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117662/selection/ab203d967d195ff54da44904f652521d55f66b5a377e2ecb487084891d40fd32" :answer-field/choices ["q-117662/selection/ab203d967d195ff54da44904f652521d55f66b5a377e2ecb487084891d40fd32" "q-117662/selection/e9fe4f903064948e90ac9e041d7548aaeba35bf685b20db89d2f19dbf50f8a32" "q-117662/selection/362d6474c6f01bbd84dd4aad1f36df5c29d2ebafec9135e07e89e7292a2cd334" "q-117662/selection/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" "q-117662/selection/aa56327b5902f25e2f7d95c792ef03ce1de9c18c97e2a74df0ef0eb1b77ad0a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117662" :question/id #uuid "8b6777ca-ff4c-593f-a186-002b5ace07e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-117662" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{-1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3x+5, & x<3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}x+13, & x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{9}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}(3x+5)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{9}(\\frac{1}{3}x+13)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+5x){|}_{-1}^{3}+(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+13x){|}_{3}^{9} \\\\  & =[3\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2}+5(3)-3\\frac{(-1)^{2}}{2}-5(-1)]+[\\frac{{9}^{2}}{6}+13(9)-\\frac{{3}^{2}}{6}-13(3)] \\\\  & =[12+20]+[12+78] \\\\  & =32+90 \\\\  & =122.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-117662/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117662"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-29742/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "1a702f00-cc31-5a7f-890f-d25bde160455" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29742/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "07e5f14d-17d1-5fa7-a0cf-bfa560f09324" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29742/selection/906fb68e52f34c93aaa89471be2f2ff4994dc9adb32c934377257fa64a54e307" :answer/id #uuid "b9916d9c-3550-58e8-b1ea-f70fe5a9003d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29742/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "cec715e0-af2e-5610-9809-8b6c86d013a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29742/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" :answer/id #uuid "f3465331-0970-50b6-83e2-d422845167c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29742/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b3c221e-24fe-5de8-a07f-d34376662b2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-29742/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer-field/choices ["q-29742/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-29742/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-29742/selection/906fb68e52f34c93aaa89471be2f2ff4994dc9adb32c934377257fa64a54e307" "q-29742/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-29742/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-29742" :question/id #uuid "f97531a0-23ba-5d30-8fd8-49fe8342841f" :question/math-academy-id "q-29742" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3x-9, & x<3 \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}-1, & x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(3x-9)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{6}(\\frac{x}{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}-9x)|}_{0}^{3}+{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-x)|}_{3}^{6} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3(3)^{2}}{2}-9(3)-\\frac{3(0)^{2}}{2}+9(0)]+[\\frac{(6)^{2}}{6}-6-\\frac{(3)^{2}}{6}+3] \\\\  & =[\\frac{27}{2}-27]+[6-6-\\frac{3}{2}+3] \\\\  & =-\\frac{27}{2}+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-29742/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-29742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-5046"] :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}4, & x<0 \\\\ -x+4, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}4\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{4}(-x+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{-3}^{0}+(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+4x){|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =[4(0)-4(-3)]+[-\\frac{(4)^{2}}{2}+4(4)+\\frac{(0)^{2}}{2}-4(0)] \\\\  & =[0+12]+[-8+16+0-0] \\\\  & =12+8 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-29734/selection/4fa830bda994f89067ddecaf273e4fa78aa4d8447b6388b70cafa0fc166e6f67" :answer/id #uuid "9b72f005-bf0f-53a1-883c-95ab5fddf5c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29734/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "37b4c793-5f8d-55f2-a868-a4f47f557656" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29734/selection/ffa26e5bcc4d7a3af71ff08758bd7169a60032efda4c49b9cffe885eed9ec1c1" :answer/id #uuid "41a5df9f-76cb-586b-911e-62d9879abe3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29734/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" :answer/id #uuid "8681517e-c7f5-5287-8622-173081258708" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29734/selection/478fd1e25e3e34a29fea1c3ec66147c061ba20da2ebcc365831518058573cd79" :answer/id #uuid "e37f9bd0-2904-5c0f-b720-dcaf12becbaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "500" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29734/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "122db715-9858-5aa2-80a6-0b91279aa5be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-29734/selection/4fa830bda994f89067ddecaf273e4fa78aa4d8447b6388b70cafa0fc166e6f67" :answer-field/choices ["q-29734/selection/4fa830bda994f89067ddecaf273e4fa78aa4d8447b6388b70cafa0fc166e6f67" "q-29734/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-29734/selection/ffa26e5bcc4d7a3af71ff08758bd7169a60032efda4c49b9cffe885eed9ec1c1" "q-29734/selection/8642573b27c8383f67a645c39127977f20fbab89a940b170bac777f18f881b9b" "q-29734/selection/478fd1e25e3e34a29fea1c3ec66147c061ba20da2ebcc365831518058573cd79"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-29734" :question/id #uuid "b781f11b-3639-5c0a-8a7a-78525a198e9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-29734" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x-9, & x<5 \\\\ \\frac{x}{5}-5, & x\\ge 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}(x-9)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{5}^{10}(\\frac{x}{5}-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-9x)|}_{0}^{5}+{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-5x)|}_{5}^{10} \\\\  & =[\\frac{(5)^{2}}{2}-9(5)-\\frac{(0)^{2}}{2}+9(0)]+[\\frac{(10)^{2}}{10}-5(10)-\\frac{(5)^{2}}{10}+5(5)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{25}{2}-45]+[10-50-\\frac{25}{10}+25] \\\\  & =-50.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-29734/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-29734"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341981/field-1/72e62c3aaaf8bb47b46edf21a05ebe176447d2d845c0a48572cff23acc77e48e" :answer/id #uuid "3cf407f2-5989-55ec-8135-061fe831e33d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-29" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341981/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "97084882-fc93-5592-8a8d-200228f92323" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341981/field-1/72e62c3aaaf8bb47b46edf21a05ebe176447d2d845c0a48572cff23acc77e48e" :answer-field/choices ["q-341981/field-1/72e62c3aaaf8bb47b46edf21a05ebe176447d2d845c0a48572cff23acc77e48e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341981" :question/id #uuid "a4321dc5-5a1f-5eae-acf4-e27f4a92f7a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-341981" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-5, & x<2, \\\\ 1, & x\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{2}(\\frac{1}{2}x-5)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{2}^{6}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-5x){|}_{-4}^{2}\\,+\\,x{|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}(2)^{2}-5(2)\\,-\\,(\\frac{1}{4}(-4)^{2}-5(-4))]\\,+\\,[\\,6-2\\,] \\\\  & =[1-10\\,-\\,(4+20)]+4 \\\\  & =[-9-24]+4 \\\\  & =-33+4 \\\\  & =-29.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341981/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec980fcb-97ed-5c60-94de-0521d9d7df27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341981"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117712/selection/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" :answer/id #uuid "f663f1be-0479-5f30-af59-c5100d945044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117712/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "e5b44619-3959-5f1b-b5b5-a9e1aeda34c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117712/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "f8e5f62a-3349-5ba3-a859-45d83a02dc8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117712/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "260baf42-ce8f-537f-9ab8-b6a551cc96f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117712/selection/98825339913b96286f9751ca67affc1b40dbfb36f8a6273cb27701f4b3f223de" :answer/id #uuid "16b2bfbd-c1bc-52e0-9629-57da1dcc0692" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117712/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0794a0c-f2fc-52b6-a93c-ad4d6e084890" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117712/selection/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" :answer-field/choices ["q-117712/selection/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" "q-117712/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-117712/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-117712/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-117712/selection/98825339913b96286f9751ca67affc1b40dbfb36f8a6273cb27701f4b3f223de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117712" :question/id #uuid "6de83420-f104-50fe-910c-fdae718dbe46" :question/math-academy-id "q-117712" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/45e506d3b6d3a2ca1a9b16a061f5c081e10b8c578796d7d4a1dfab6e6f793520.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of three line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-5}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We divide the interval of integration into $4$ regions: the line segment for $x\\in [-5,-3],$ the line segment for $x\\in [-3,-1],$ the line segment for $x\\in (-1,1),$ and the line segment for $x\\in [1,4].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-5}^{-3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{4}}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-5,-3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,-1].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-1,1).$ The corresponding region is a square, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,4].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =4.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{4}=-4.5.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3}-{A}_{4} \\\\  & =2-2+4-4.5 \\\\  & =-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-117712/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117712"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338327/field-1/a00dffabf29685084c0b6de6e66784f365038b80a482b9e8fb5db4101fc238a6" :answer/id #uuid "9ef69d82-c2fa-59b5-97c1-d769b44d02e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338327/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a37dd813-ec61-5ea2-8e32-14acea737276" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338327/field-1/a00dffabf29685084c0b6de6e66784f365038b80a482b9e8fb5db4101fc238a6" :answer-field/choices ["q-338327/field-1/a00dffabf29685084c0b6de6e66784f365038b80a482b9e8fb5db4101fc238a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338327" :question/id #uuid "df7f13fa-a1e0-5a8e-88c8-5c84f775afbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-338327" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/04a0e2e6bf3aab5454192f6dc46ca9cae306e08ca96ea600bfa87600ef2b4369.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of three line segments. Then,\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of three parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-6,-2],$ the line segment for $x\\in (-2,1],$ and the line segment for $x\\in (1,4].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-6}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-6,-2].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+5)4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-2,1].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =bh \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (1,4].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4+1)3 \\\\  & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =12+6+7.5 \\\\  & =25.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-338327/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338327"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338474/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "d5243a4d-dcd4-5ca5-b407-72cd6f66fa52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338474/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "e475fc43-846c-5b63-af16-ceb7d14d5d17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338474/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "72b15476-f1a9-5622-b285-fa765bfc2df6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338474/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-338474/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-338474/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338474" :question/id #uuid "4cace43a-76f0-54d2-8e26-2c393b0daefe" :question/math-academy-id "q-338474" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/44d4c8752c83db3b64b75b7b115902474856391ea87a21de1466a166816db929.png)\n\nThe graph $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Then,\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We divide the interval of integration into $3$ regions: the horizontal segment for $x\\in [-4,-1],$ the sloped segment for $x\\in (-1,0],$ and the sloped segment for $x\\in [0,3].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,-1].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =bh \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-1,0].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle below the $x$-axis, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we subtract its area.\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =6-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-338474/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338474"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49212"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/69669250982a974c17cba2d70f27077f9c523ef184ff3f09650ea8d439428589.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We divide the interval of integration into $3$ regions: the line segment for $x\\in [-3,-1],$ the line segment for $x\\in [-1,0),$ and the line segment for $x\\in [0,3].$ Therefore, we write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,-1].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,0).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-0.5.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,3].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2)(3) \\\\  & =4.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =2-0.5+4.5 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-86167/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "b7336e5b-19d7-54c3-9d8b-d527be2ebcef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86167/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "0f693360-1d6e-522c-bf4d-389e29b65467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86167/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "f207fce9-e9d3-58ed-9d49-136a7c6a537e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86167/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c93a060d-f9ad-5cad-802e-a562e8258701" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86167/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "c87eeb99-3e4f-5c43-a2a9-9444183f192b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86167/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "42712ed9-5a3c-5ef9-80d4-fbb4396ae6ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86167/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-86167/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-86167/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-86167/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-86167/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-86167/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86167" :question/id #uuid "54902dd1-a8a7-5a9c-9e30-07d51d056c94" :question/math-academy-id "q-86167" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/bac953cd2389ef36b415dcdce87730f244958ef0fe2f67911878c5cb3bfcafc6.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We divide the interval of integration into $3$ regions: the line segment for $x\\in [-4,0],$ the line segment for $x\\in (0,4],$ and the line segment for $x\\in [4,6].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{3}}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,0].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+3)(4) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (0,4].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [4,6].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{3}=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}-{A}_{3} \\\\  & =8+4-1 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-86167/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86167"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49209/selection/45c72e34a6abe2dcabcf59d74e56a70f015c149bb49dc887418bca5d8f111f58" :answer/id #uuid "3093ca09-ff01-5b89-a6df-52d1b6cabd3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi +12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49209/selection/78539d8fcff73402fc05b0438c865ec11fd810c4fd8819a13256a93a83de13d2" :answer/id #uuid "5cc3a64b-5a64-51aa-9538-347ccbe3e387" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi +10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49209/selection/ecf16c0ad3f8fff50f8f0e4efd86eb88c2dd3011efd658097a817cee3720e770" :answer/id #uuid "0f2c0275-349c-5c5d-a679-d3c3abf7264e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi +14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49209/selection/3eb5d62dc78eb5ed512d8993c7660f3f31eb42d30a9531545439fc00523550f9" :answer/id #uuid "6e1c4e0a-a5f4-54b9-8263-b4a09d83cbe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi +16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49209/selection/60ebe930695a4094c7816d4e2898d9cd63a187a2b7d40d0d8a7ceede221dd00b" :answer/id #uuid "9b8fc3b0-7f3c-5b90-8142-b8a2d1469e7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi +11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49209/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "210868a4-a578-5362-9e93-f091d1cfdb9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49209/selection/ecf16c0ad3f8fff50f8f0e4efd86eb88c2dd3011efd658097a817cee3720e770" :answer-field/choices ["q-49209/selection/45c72e34a6abe2dcabcf59d74e56a70f015c149bb49dc887418bca5d8f111f58" "q-49209/selection/78539d8fcff73402fc05b0438c865ec11fd810c4fd8819a13256a93a83de13d2" "q-49209/selection/ecf16c0ad3f8fff50f8f0e4efd86eb88c2dd3011efd658097a817cee3720e770" "q-49209/selection/3eb5d62dc78eb5ed512d8993c7660f3f31eb42d30a9531545439fc00523550f9" "q-49209/selection/60ebe930695a4094c7816d4e2898d9cd63a187a2b7d40d0d8a7ceede221dd00b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49209" :question/id #uuid "ed812b2f-487d-5fe1-bd24-af0e5cfc7e1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-49209" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/78500fa72c8f6aa49d95f34b88ce71ec79304203d7646200e98c311d8610200f.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of \n${\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of $2$ parts: the arc of the semi-circle for $x\\in [-4,0]$ and the line segment for $x\\in (0,3).$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={{{\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,0].$ The corresponding region is a combination of a semi-circle of radius $2$ and a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi {r}^{2})+bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2})+4(2) \\\\  & =2\\pi +8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (0,3).$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+3)(3) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =(2\\pi +8)+6 \\\\  & =2\\pi +14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-49209/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49209"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-14785"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/824f039d5f015a2cd2165cfd469c44e7f3e5a0cda6416964ec91d57de4ca06eb.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of \n${\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of $3$ parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-3,1),$ the arc of the semi-circle for $x\\in [1,3],$ and the line segment for $x\\in [3,4].$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThe $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,1).$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =b\\cdot h \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-4.\n$$\n\nThe $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,3].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle of radius of $1,$ so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,4].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{3}=-\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}-{A}_{3} \\\\  & =-4+\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-339264/field-1/beab779f62ea4e149d6f96c3934c6aa37380b11d0fb4afaebde5b2af06977629" :answer/id #uuid "023fe5b1-a8b7-522e-b3f5-8df651e50105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8+2\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339264/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ec77927-8866-56a5-a3b4-a52a1fa9c85d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339264/field-1/beab779f62ea4e149d6f96c3934c6aa37380b11d0fb4afaebde5b2af06977629" :answer-field/choices ["q-339264/field-1/beab779f62ea4e149d6f96c3934c6aa37380b11d0fb4afaebde5b2af06977629"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339264" :question/id #uuid "e542677b-970f-5562-ac6a-54a112381d14" :question/math-academy-id "q-339264" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/db123092734fe2d84dacd2da2d005d001aadb673d1ad7f30c9527ef9f5a8ba7c.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-5}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of $2$ parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-5,-1)$ and the arc of the semi-circle for $x\\in [-1,3].$ Using the additive property of integrals, we write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-5}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-5,-1).$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+3)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,3].$ The corresponding region is a semicircle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot (2)^{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =8+2\\pi  \\\\  & =8+2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339264/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339264"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86178/selection/829358ad7c0722497dfcccb7b404dcd13c0c4d3720a0477c1f98072dfac7d83b" :answer/id #uuid "2df1dce3-027e-5e65-8748-5e0d62b6f721" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12+2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86178/selection/dae884962c05f0e27fa2fa1ad089881c97735b0a9c68f59607ff70d630735f08" :answer/id #uuid "936814f3-5e8f-5cd5-affd-6445a2184354" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21-2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86178/selection/5cbe2b74ca6cebdd508e51c9bc58294ccf11105d17da0bf613763e3e8e8a1b9c" :answer/id #uuid "ffd9397b-0e81-5ad6-a8e4-78ba1876c415" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14+2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86178/selection/4818acd05aadac16b30d27e7caadb6ddf48be2f85704c5051f16eedce5fe13c8" :answer/id #uuid "424d89dc-d6a1-5599-83f5-5608ad40b255" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18-4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86178/selection/49b29d2922d547c0450afe2b723feaa4a7b598aba61bd5929e98baa099779d8f" :answer/id #uuid "0ac2144b-27b0-551c-a438-7c7dcb4c0784" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19-2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86178/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d47c3dc4-aea7-58ff-8bd3-9baf57e6312f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86178/selection/dae884962c05f0e27fa2fa1ad089881c97735b0a9c68f59607ff70d630735f08" :answer-field/choices ["q-86178/selection/829358ad7c0722497dfcccb7b404dcd13c0c4d3720a0477c1f98072dfac7d83b" "q-86178/selection/dae884962c05f0e27fa2fa1ad089881c97735b0a9c68f59607ff70d630735f08" "q-86178/selection/5cbe2b74ca6cebdd508e51c9bc58294ccf11105d17da0bf613763e3e8e8a1b9c" "q-86178/selection/4818acd05aadac16b30d27e7caadb6ddf48be2f85704c5051f16eedce5fe13c8" "q-86178/selection/49b29d2922d547c0450afe2b723feaa4a7b598aba61bd5929e98baa099779d8f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86178" :question/id #uuid "4401c384-957e-5e9f-8c94-3a563dbdfad0" :question/math-academy-id "q-86178" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/8f9b82ba9e1ed640aedd6f67118beef2d88c419bbd046171cca5b527c2b407a5.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of \n${\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of $3$ parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-4,-2]$, the arc of the semi-circle for $x\\in [-2,2),$ and the line segment for $x\\in (2,4].$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,-2].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =bh \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,2).$ The corresponding region is a combination of an inverted semi-circle of radius $2$ and a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =bh-\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =4(3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\pi (2)^{2} \\\\  & =12-2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (2,4].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =6+12-2\\pi +3 \\\\  & =21-2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-86178/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86178"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117985/selection/d691192ac5f3fcdd748d24f16ee6769efe9ccc2c7060f927e5aed5f483c71465" :answer/id #uuid "e8259267-b52c-58a7-bf17-76ea41a6551c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117985/selection/0fb978d2b1ce374ae0f1700c585078833e85991af693baf7445a5e2dc6cdf6cc" :answer/id #uuid "8ab64d5e-cd64-53d0-a3cb-2c1ec5159f33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117985/selection/6faadb725876d2cb4b4b22fd8cb48065449f531124b5b1865dc76fc903e4a1a3" :answer/id #uuid "3496e2fb-d5c9-56f1-96e9-aa339c0faf2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6-2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117985/selection/1a2c3881891ab7eca8aa4af8d7002d84b8252f633df18da1be453e64ebd8a8b4" :answer/id #uuid "1552a599-9efc-5d5a-8c48-092e46377238" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117985/selection/83cb4a7f4415017398e13c6fbf099c19c33ef318581dcf4ddd43ceb6a874b521" :answer/id #uuid "da7d4477-972e-53e3-a43e-d86035ceb85a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117985/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "df8aa656-260b-58f4-a39c-8617ee5002a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117985/selection/6faadb725876d2cb4b4b22fd8cb48065449f531124b5b1865dc76fc903e4a1a3" :answer-field/choices ["q-117985/selection/d691192ac5f3fcdd748d24f16ee6769efe9ccc2c7060f927e5aed5f483c71465" "q-117985/selection/0fb978d2b1ce374ae0f1700c585078833e85991af693baf7445a5e2dc6cdf6cc" "q-117985/selection/6faadb725876d2cb4b4b22fd8cb48065449f531124b5b1865dc76fc903e4a1a3" "q-117985/selection/1a2c3881891ab7eca8aa4af8d7002d84b8252f633df18da1be453e64ebd8a8b4" "q-117985/selection/83cb4a7f4415017398e13c6fbf099c19c33ef318581dcf4ddd43ceb6a874b521"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117985" :question/id #uuid "835aaac1-7356-5c01-b2df-661cf4a5872f" :question/math-academy-id "q-117985" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/03a826b548db2731a6854327d6e11dcc5147d5c21db93f0b17b6b131e5163efc.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of \n${\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of $3$ parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-5,-1],$ the arc of the semi-circle for $x\\in [-1,3],$ and the line segment for $x\\in (3,5].$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-5}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThe $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-5,-1].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,3].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle of radius of $2,$ so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{2}=-2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (3,5].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{3}=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}-{A}_{3} \\\\  & =8-2\\pi -2 \\\\  & =6-2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117985/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117985"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-432"] :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of $\\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^5 f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3, & x<0 \\\\ 2x+3, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}3\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{5}(2x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x{|}_{-2}^{0}+({x}^{2}+3x){|}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =[3(0)-3(-2)]+[({5}^{2}+3(5))-({0}^{2}+3(0))] \\\\  & =6+25+15 \\\\  & =46.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-433"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/ad45cbdcd126df931f1a35c60ca12b45d520a2a0a5cddf4fa012c0515d3024c7.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Find the value of $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{4} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of two parts: the line segment for $x \\in [0,2)$ and the line segment for $x \\in [2,4].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{4} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = \\underbrace{\\int_{0}^{2} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x}_{A_1} + \\underbrace{\\int_{2}^{4} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x}_{-A_2}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x \\in [0,2).$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =bh \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x \\in [2,4].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n\\int_{2}^{4} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x =-A_2 = -2.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2} \\\\  & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-434"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010574/assets/36c6a1c84e0b0c32a5fd35fd422645f60340da6d205dd8cc31054cd558c2f5f9.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of $\\displaystyle \\int_{-4}^4 f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of four parts: the arc of a semi-circle for $x\\in [-4,0],$ a line segment for $x\\in (0,2),$ a line segment for $x\\in (2,4],$ and the point at $x=2.$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={{{\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{2}}+0+{{{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x \\in [-4,0].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle with a radius of $2,$ so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x \\in (0,2).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{2} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -A_2 = -2.\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x \\in (2,4].$  The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\pi -2+2 \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
